course: dictionary
lesson: 15721
title: Words for paths and progress
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trajectory is the curved path that something follows when it is thrown, kicked or fired through the air. Think of a football flying up and over a hedge: the curve it makes is its trajectory. «The ball's trajectory took it right over the goalkeeper's head.»
explain: The word has a second meaning too. It can be the direction something develops over time. «Our club's trajectory this season is upward, with more wins every month.» Nothing is flying here. The club is getting better step by step, and that path over time is its trajectory.
explain: Trajectory often appears in science and maths, where the path of a thrown object is an arch shape called a parabola, because gravity pulls it down. Rockets and space probes also follow trajectories to reach planets. To decide which meaning fits, ask: is something moving through the air, or changing over time?
fact: Trajectory is a noun. One trajectory, and more than one trajectory.
fact: A trajectory is the curved path of a thrown, kicked or fired object.
fact: The path of a ball, arrow or rocket is often arch-shaped, called a parabola.
fact: «On an upward trajectory» means getting better or bigger over time.
fact: You can «change trajectory», which means to change the direction something is heading.
exercise: «The arrow followed a high, curved trajectory before it landed in the field.» What is a trajectory? | The bright colour of the sky at sunset | *The curved path an object follows through the air | A special bow made from wood
exercise: «Prices have been on an upward trajectory all year.» What does trajectory mean here? | A loud noise from a far-off hill | A thick, heavy coat | *The direction something is developing over time
exercise: Mia kicks a ball over the wall. Which word names the curved path the ball follows? | sandwich | blanket | *trajectory | puddle
test: «The rocket changed trajectory after it passed the Moon.» What does changed trajectory mean? | It was painted a new colour | It lost its colour and went dark | *It changed the direction it was heading in | It turned round and landed back at home
test: Which sentence uses trajectory to mean a direction over time? | I ate a cheese sandwich for lunch | The dog barked at the postman | *The company's trajectory has been steadily upward for ten years
exam: Which is the best meaning of trajectory? | A small animal that lives in a burrow | *A curved path through the air, or the direction something develops over time | A shiny metal tool used for cutting bread
